This package includes prebuilt software from the official Alpine Linux
minirootfs. Its components retain their upstream copyright and license terms.
The root filesystem archive is a binary distribution, not corresponding source.

Primary components include:

- apk-tools and libapk: GPL-2.0-only
  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/apk-tools
- BusyBox: GPL-2.0-only
  https://busybox.net/
- musl: MIT
  https://musl.libc.org/
- OpenSSL: Apache-2.0
  https://openssl-library.org/
- zlib: Zlib
  https://zlib.net/

The manifest pins the official archive URL and SHA-512. The build output includes
runtime-packages.txt; the runtime database at /lib/apk/db/installed also records
component versions, licenses, origins, and aports commit identifiers.

Alpine package recipes and source references:
https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/packages
https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/

The apk-tools GPL text is included in the image under
/usr/share/licenses/apk-tools/LICENSE. Distributors must include all required
component notices and provide corresponding source or another arrangement
permitted by the applicable licenses.
